   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the local finance law, in relation to the period of probable\nusefulness of zero-emission school buses",
    "basePrintNo": "S9292",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9292-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 50,
       "fullName": "John Mannion",
       "imgName": "1315_John_Mannion.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1498,
       "sessionMemberId": 2048,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "MANNION"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1604, 1709 & 3602, Ed L; amd §11.00, Loc Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Local Finance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9292\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the local finance law, in relation to the period of\nprobable usefulness of zero-emission school buses\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo change the amortization period of electric school buses from twelve\nyears to eight years.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: amends Local Finance Law § 11(29a) to change the amortization\nperiod for the purchase of an EV school bus from 12 years to 8 years.\n\nSection 2: establishes the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nStarting in 2027, school districts in New York will be required to\npurchase zero-emission school buses to replace standard diesel buses.\nDistricts receive transportation aid from the state as partial\nreimbursement for certain transportation expenses, including the\npurchase of new buses. Aid for the purchases of buses if paid out over a\nperiod of several years known as the amortization period. This helps\ndistricts pay for ongoing maintenance costs and reflects the fact that\nmost districts bond to purchase buses.\n\nUnder current law, the amortization period for zero-emission school\nbuses is set at 12 years. In contrast, diesel buses have an amortization\nperiod of five years. This legislation would change the amortization\nperiod for zero-emission school buses to 8 years to more accurately\nreflect the expected life of electric school buses.  Electric bus\nbatteries often have a warranty that only last 7 or 8 years. And zero\nemission buses have many features, like diesel buses, that are subject\nto rust and other wear and tear that limits their useful lifetime.\n\nThis bill is a common sense change that will make it easier for school\ndistricts to navigate the transition to 100% electric bus fleets.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of July next succeeding the date\non which it shall have become a law.\n",
